      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was officially founded in 1884 by Scottish immigrant David Mackie, who helped plat the community and later became the first president of the Scammon State Bank.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/scammon_kansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The local railroad history group, Heart of the Heartlands, has restored the old Carona depot into a museum, preserving regional rail heritage.",
